{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The route deviation is ESTABLISHED on this trip's own trace. The governing figure is gps_trace.trace_distance_km at 28.18 km, measured against a platform optimal of 22.4 km recorded on the trip record at booking: an excess of 5.78 km, or 25.8% of the optimal. POL-RD-01 requires both gates to pass — more than 20% of the optimal and more than 0.8 km absolute — and both do, so the deviation stands. I cite the trace distance, not the rounded 28.2 km convenience copy on the trip record, because POL-RD-01 makes the trace figure govern where the two disagree.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00115", "EV-TRIP-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes and this dispute is therefore rulable on it. It carries 229 fixes at a 10-second sample interval, 100% coverage, an empty gaps array and a maximum gap of 0 seconds across the full 21:10:00 to 21:48:00 window. It meets no limb (a), (b) or (c) of POL-RD-07, so the deviation may be established on the gps_trace alone, no independent corroboration is required, and the mandatory escalation route in POL-RD-10(3) is closed rather than triggered.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's initial burden under POL-RD-08 is discharged. The trip_record, the gps_trace and the fare_breakdown all carry the same trip identifier, TRP-00115, and the trace's first fix at 21:10:00 corresponds to the recorded start on the same booking whose pickup is Marina Bay Financial Centre Tower 3; the excess of 5.78 km is measured from that unimpaired trace and clears the POL-RD-01 threshold. rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 0, so the extra corroboration limb of POL-RD-08 is not engaged and the rider's claim does not even need it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00115", "EV-GPS-00115", "EV-FARE-00115", "EV-RPROF-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's explanation — 'CTE northbound was heavy so I used the KPE and TPE' — is an external-traffic assertion that fails for want of the only artifact that could carry it. The bundle's traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-00115-01, is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 (issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT): no LTA advisory covers the CTE, KPE or TPE in the 21:06-21:48 window. POL-RD-03 requires an advisory that names a road the optimal route traverses and carries an overlapping validity window; that comparison cannot be run on this record, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and under POL-RD-08 and POL-RD-13 the assertion carries no weight and reduces no excess. Because the driver names no advisory ID, the absence is a gap in the bundle rather than a POL-RD-10(5) contradiction, and no escalation follows from it. The same statement is also a concession on the facts the rider needs: he does not dispute the route he drove, and he offers no evidence ID for the congestion he blames.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00115-01", "EV-CHAT-00115", "EV-FARE-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no rider instruction that could exonerate the detour, so POL-RD-04 is unavailable to the driver. The whole chat is two messages: 'CTE very heavy boss, i go KPE then TPE', sent by the DRIVER at 21:14:10, and the rider's two-letter reply 'ok' at 21:14:50. POL-RD-04(a) requires the instruction to come from the rider and POL-RD-04(c) requires it to identify a place or road specifically enough to act on; the first limb fails outright, waypoint_hint is null on both messages so the corroboration test cannot even be run, and an acknowledgement of a diversion the driver had already announced is not a request for one. The excess is therefore not attributable to the rider and is not excluded.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The fare model decides what is recoverable, and I put the rider's case on the clause that actually governs it. fare_breakdown.fare_model is UPFRONT_QUOTE with quoted_fare_sgd 34.50, so POL-RD-11 governs and POL-RD-02 does not run: the rider was fixed at the quote on distance and time, and I do not ask for the 5.78 km of excess to be refunded as distance, because POL-RD-11 gives no distance remedy on an upfront trip. What stays live are POL-RD-11(a), the amount by which charged_total exceeds the quote plus the properly chargeable pass-through lines, and POL-RD-11(b), the pass-through correction for lines the trace never crossed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fare_model",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas) line of SGD 2.00 is a phantom charge and a billing-integrity failure. The line is marked on_optimal_route false, and the trace's closest approach to that gantry is 5,419.3 m — the very first fix, at 21:10:00 — against the 250 m crossing radius POL-RD-09(4) applies. The rider was billed for that gantry at 21:26:05, from a route that never came within five kilometres of it. Under POL-RD-09(4) the line is refunded in full as a standalone correction, available whether or not a deviation is established, and recorded as a billing-integrity referral. Because that is the only unmatched line in the fare_breakdown, POL-RD-10(8) is expressly not engaged, and the money should move rather than be held.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00115", "EV-GPS-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-10"],
      "relies_on": "derived.erp_gantry_proximity.lines[1].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The arithmetic is not discretionary. charged_total is 39.00 and the quote is 34.50. The only ERP line properly chargeable under POL-RD-09 is the KPE (Defu Flyover towards ECP) gantry at 2.50: it lies on the optimal route and the trace crosses it at 44.5 m. There is no airport surcharge (the trip neither originates at an airport) and the waiting_time_fee is 0.00. So 39.00 - 34.50 - 2.50 = 2.00, which is the refund; rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 it remains 2.00 — the same figure the fare record's own money block publishes as pol_rd_11_remedy. POL-RD-11(b) adds nothing on top of that, because the off-route AYE line is already excluded from the properly chargeable total and adding it again would refund it twice.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00115", "EV-GPS-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.pol_rd_11_remedy",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Finally, none of POL-RD-10's escalation triggers fires, and the rider should not have to wait for money that is plainly owed. The identifiers all match TRP-00115 (10(2)); the trace is unimpaired at 100% coverage with no gaps (10(3)); the refund of 2.00 is far below both charged_total and the SGD 150.00 ceiling (10(6)); the single unmatched charge line is the AYE gantry refunded under POL-RD-09(4), which 10(8) excludes by its own terms; and 10(5) is not engaged because no party cited an advisory identifier. fare_breakdown.payment_status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00, so on this rider-filed dispute NO_ACTION would simply leave the whole 39.00 standing. The correct outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 2.00 to the filing rider, together with the billing-integrity referral POL-RD-09(4) requires.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00115", "EV-GPS-00115", "EV-ADVIS-00115-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 2.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4): billing integrity — the AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas) ERP line of SGD 2.00 was charged on a route the trace never came within 5,419 m of; refunded in full as a standalone pass-through correction."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Both sides agree on the central facts, and the money turns on the fare model, not on the driving. This was an UPFRONT_QUOTE trip: EV-FARE-00115 shows fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE with quoted_fare_sgd 34.50. Under POL-RD-11 your distance and time charges were fixed at booking and cannot be re-opened, so the rider's request to 'refund the extra distance' fails on the fare model itself. The deviation is nonetheless ESTABLISHED under POL-RD-01 — the governing trace figure on EV-GPS-00115 is trace_distance_km 28.18 against the booked optimal 22.4 km, an excess of 5.78 km / 25.8%, clearing both the 20% and 0.8 km gates — but it is not MATERIAL (neither over 50% nor over 8.0 km), so no POL-RD-02 computation runs and no POL-RD-06 FULL_REFUND uplift is available. The refund therefore comes only from the ERP lines. You were charged 39.00, which is 4.50 above the 34.50 quote. Of that: the KPE (Defu Flyover towards ECP) line of 2.50 is properly chargeable — it lies on the optimal route and the 100%-coverage trace crosses it at 44.5 m, inside the 250 m radius — while the AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas) line of 2.00 is a phantom charge: it is not on the optimal route and the trace's closest approach is 5,419 m, at the first fix, against a gantry the receipt says was charged at 21:26:05. Under POL-RD-09(4) that line is refunded in full as a standalone billing-integrity correction, available whether or not a deviation exists. The arithmetic, read off EV-FARE-00115, is charged_total 39.00 − quoted_fare 34.50 − the only properly chargeable pass-through (KPE 2.50; airport surcharge 0.00, waiting_time_fee 0.00) = 2.00, already a multiple of 0.05, and identical to the remedy the fare record's own money block publishes. POL-RD-11(b) adds nothing on top of that, because the AYE line is already excluded from the properly chargeable total and counting it twice would refund it twice. On the driver's explanation that CTE traffic forced the KPE/TPE route: the bundle's only traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-00115-01, is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT (no LTA advisory covers the CTE, KPE or TPE in the 21:06–21:48 window), so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and under POL-RD-08 and POL-RD-13 the assertion carries no weight and reduces no excess; it costs you nothing here because the fare was fixed anyway. POL-RD-04 is likewise unavailable: the only chat traffic is the driver's own 21:14:10 diversion notice and the rider's 'ok', the rider gave no instruction, and waypoint_hint is null, so no distance is excluded on that ground. No escalation applies: the trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07(a)–(c) (100% coverage, 229 fixes, no gaps), the trip identifiers all match TRP-00115, and the single unmatched charge line is exactly the one POL-RD-09(4) refunds, which POL-RD-10(8) excludes by its own terms. No repeat-deviation pattern exists under POL-RD-06 (deviation_flags_90d 1 over 523 completed trips, below both limbs), so there is no FULL_REFUND uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral; the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is context-only under POL-GEN-01 and was given no weight. The one referral is mandatory under POL-RD-09(4) for the phantom AYE line. Confidence is 0.95: the deciding facts are carried by EV-FARE-00115 and EV-GPS-00115, both at weight_multiplier 1.0, so nothing is capped below the 0.70 floor. The monetary effect of 2.00 does not exceed the 8.00 execution threshold on the policy, so it executes automatically on issue. This differs from precedents P-0001 and P-0002, which shared POL-RD-01/POL-RD-02/POL-RD-08: here the fare is upfront-quoted, so POL-RD-11 governs and no distance refund is available."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Finally, none of POL-RD-10's escalation triggers fires, and the rider should not have to wait for money that is plainly owed. The identifiers all match TRP-00115 (10(2)); the trace is unimpaired at 100% coverage with no gaps (10(3)); the refund of 2.00 is far below both charged_total and the SGD 150.00 ceiling (10(6)); the single unmatched charge line is the AYE gantry refunded under POL-RD-09(4), which 10(8) excludes by its own terms; and 10(5) is not engaged because no party cited an advisory identifier. fare_breakdown.payment_status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00, so on this rider-filed dispute NO_ACTION would simply leave the whole 39.00 standing. The correct outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 2.00 to the filing rider, together with the billing-integrity referral POL-RD-09(4) requires.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00115-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 2.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing integrity: refund in full the phantom AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas) gantry line of SGD 2.00, which the trace never crossed and which is not on the optimal route, and correct the fare ledger so the gantry is not billed for this trip."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider: you are partly right, and you get back the charge the driver never incurred. You were on an upfront-quoted fare — EV-FARE-00115 shows fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE with a quoted fare of SGD 34.50 — so the distance and time charges were fixed at booking, and POL-RD-11 does not allow a refund of the extra distance however large it was. Your route complaint is nonetheless well founded: EV-GPS-00115 records a trace distance of 28.18 km against a booked optimal of 22.4 km, an excess of 5.78 km (25.8%), which passes both POL-RD-01 gates (>20% and >0.8 km) and establishes a deviation — it is simply not a distance refund on this fare model. What is refunded is the AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas) line of SGD 2.00 charged at 21:26:05: the gantry is not on the optimal route and the trace's closest approach is 5,419 m, so under POL-RD-09(4) it is refunded in full as a standalone billing correction, available whether or not a deviation exists. The arithmetic: charged_total 39.00 − quoted fare 34.50 − the only properly chargeable ERP line, the KPE (Defu Flyover towards ECP) gantry at 2.50, which is on the optimal route and which the trace crosses at 44.5 m (no airport surcharge, waiting time fee 0.00) = 2.00, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 and unchanged at SGD 2.00. That is part of the SGD 6.00 you contested, hence a PARTIAL_REFUND. To the driver: the KPE charge of SGD 2.50 stays with you, because it is a proper pass-through you actually crossed. Your explanation that the CTE was heavy carries no weight: it asserts an external traffic cause, the only traffic advisory for the window (EV-ADVIS-00115-01) is MISSING at weight_multiplier 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and under POL-RD-13 and POL-RD-08 an uncited traffic assertion neither reduces the measured excess nor supplies an adjusted optimal route. Your in-app message at 21:14:10 announcing the KPE/TPE reroute is not a rider instruction — the rider's 'ok' acknowledges your message and does not request a detour — so POL-RD-04 exonerates no part of the excess. No repeat-deviation pattern is found: deviation_flags_90d is 1 against completed_trips_90d 523, below both POL-RD-06 thresholds, so there is no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral, and prior_deviation_flags is a lifetime counter that POL-GEN-01 forbids using. The AYE line is a ledger error, not a finding about your route. Evidence and escalation: every artifact carrying the decision (EV-TRIP-00115, EV-GPS-00115, EV-FARE-00115, EV-CHAT-00115) is at weight 1.0, the one impaired artifact (the missing advisory, weight 0.0) carries no fact, and no POL-RD-10 trigger fires — the identifiers all match TRP-00115, the trace is unimpaired at 100% coverage with no gaps, and the single unmatched charge line is the one POL-RD-09(4) refunds, which POL-RD-10(8) excludes. As this ruling's monetary effect (SGD 2.00) is below the execution threshold, it executes automatically, and either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04. A claim the rider's advocate advanced on escalation was discarded by the referee for not disclosing the missing advisory's issue code; the escalation conclusion is reached here on the kept claims and the record. Precedents P-0001 and P-0002 share this case's PARTIAL_REFUND value but turn on a POL-RD-02 distance recomputation; this trip is upfront-quoted, so the refund here comes from a POL-RD-11 pass-through correction instead."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Finally, none of POL-RD-10's escalation triggers fires, and the rider should not have to wait for money that is plainly owed. The identifiers all match TRP-00115 (10(2)); the trace is unimpaired at 100% coverage with no gaps (10(3)); the refund of 2.00 is far below both charged_total and the SGD 150.00 ceiling (10(6)); the single unmatched charge line is the AYE gantry refunded under POL-RD-09(4), which 10(8) excludes by its own terms; and 10(5) is not engaged because no party cited an advisory identifier. fare_breakdown.payment_status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00, so on this rider-filed dispute NO_ACTION would simply leave the whole 39.00 standing. The correct outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 2.00 to the filing rider, together with the billing-integrity referral POL-RD-09(4) requires.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00115-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 2.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity review: the AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas) gantry line of SGD 2.00 was charged at 21:26:05 on EV-FARE-00115 although the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00115) never comes closer than 5,419 m to that gantry and the gantry is not on the optimal route. The line is refunded in full and the ledger entry is referred for billing-integrity review."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties. This was an upfront-quoted trip. EV-FARE-00115 records fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE with quoted_fare_sgd 34.50 and charged_total 39.00, so POL-RD-11 governs and the distance and time charges were fixed at booking. The excess is real — the governing trace figure on EV-GPS-00115 is trace_distance_km 28.18 km against the booked optimal of 22.4 km on EV-TRIP-00115, an excess of 5.78 km or 25.8%, which clears both POL-RD-01 gates — but on an upfront fare it is not refundable on distance or time, and the rider's demand to refund the extra distance fails on the fare model itself. Nothing is owed for the detour on those lines. The driver's explanation of heavy CTE traffic is also not accepted as reducing anything: the bundle's only traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-00115-01, is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT (no LTA advisory covers the CTE, KPE or TPE in the 21:06-21:48 window), so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and under POL-RD-13 and POL-RD-08 the assertion carries no weight. That gap does not escalate the case: the driver cited no advisory identifier, and the upfront fare means the failed excuse costs him nothing on distance or time. What is refundable is the difference between what was charged and what was properly chargeable. Of the 39.00, 34.50 is the quote and 2.50 is the KPE (Defu Flyover towards ECP) gantry, which lies on the optimal route and which the trace passes at 44.5 m — a properly chargeable pass-through under POL-RD-09 that stays with the driver. The AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas) line of 2.00 is not chargeable: the trace's closest approach to that gantry is 5,419 m, over five kilometres away, and the gantry is not on the optimal route. The arithmetic is 39.00 - 34.50 - 2.50 = 2.00, refunded in full and rounded up to SGD 2.00; the fare record publishes the same figure. The AYE line is a billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4), refunded as a standalone correction and recorded as the referral above; that referral does not delay or displace the money. No repeat-deviation pattern is found: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1 against completed_trips_90d of 523, below both POL-RD-06 limbs, so no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral follow; the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags may not be substituted for the trailing-90-day figure under POL-GEN-01. The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes (229 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0), the trip identifiers all read TRP-00115, the AYE line is the POL-RD-09(4) carve-out in POL-RD-10(8), and no other POL-RD-10 trigger fires, so the case is decidable rather than escalated. Confidence is 0.90, resting on EV-FARE-00115 and EV-GPS-00115, both at weight_multiplier 1.0. The refund of SGD 2.00 is below the SGD 8.00 automatic execution threshold and executes on issue. This differs from earlier route-deviation closures sharing POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-08 because those ran the POL-RD-02 metered recomputation, whereas this trip's fare_model is UPFRONT_QUOTE and only the POL-RD-11 pass-through correction is available. Either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Finally, none of POL-RD-10's escalation triggers fires, and the rider should not have to wait for money that is plainly owed. The identifiers all match TRP-00115 (10(2)); the trace is unimpaired at 100% coverage with no gaps (10(3)); the refund of 2.00 is far below both charged_total and the SGD 150.00 ceiling (10(6)); the single unmatched charge line is the AYE gantry refunded under POL-RD-09(4), which 10(8) excludes by its own terms; and 10(5) is not engaged because no party cited an advisory identifier. fare_breakdown.payment_status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00, so on this rider-filed dispute NO_ACTION would simply leave the whole 39.00 standing. The correct outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 2.00 to the filing rider, together with the billing-integrity referral POL-RD-09(4) requires.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00115-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}
